# 2LLazy job ingestion from cron — the alternative to the systemd timer in
# deploy/2llazy-ingest.timer. Use one or the other, not both.
#
# Install as a system crontab (note the user column, which a personal
# `crontab -e` file does not have):
#
#   sudo cp deploy/crontab.example /etc/cron.d/2llazy
#   sudo chmod 0644 /etc/cron.d/2llazy
#
# Then pick ONE of the two blocks below and delete the other.
#
# ── REPLACE: the paths, the user, the countries, and MAILTO ─────────────────
#
# Notes that apply to both:
#
#   * Three runs a day is right. Ingestion is incremental — a repeat run only
#     fetches what the board says has changed — so running it hourly costs the
#     boards bandwidth and gains you almost nothing.
#   * :17 rather than :00. Every cron on every machine fires on the hour.
#   * flock is what keeps two runs from overlapping. The ingester is safe to
#     run beside the web app; it is not safe to run beside itself, because two
#     copies contend on the same rows and crawl every board twice.
#   * Countries run one after another inside the same lock, for the same
#     reason: the worldwide boards are shared between them.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
# Cron mails anything the job writes to stdout or stderr. The ingester prints a
# per-board summary, which is worth reading. Blank it out to stay quiet.
MAILTO=you@example.com

# ── Block 1: Docker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runs the `ingest` service from docker-compose.yml, which reads .env from the
# same directory. Needs a user in the docker group (or root).

17 5,13,21 * * *  root  cd /opt/2llazy && flock -n /run/lock/2llazy-ingest.lock sh -c 'docker compose run --rm ingest --country CZ; docker compose run --rm ingest --country DE' >> /var/log/2llazy/ingest.log 2>&1

# ── Block 2: bare metal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `set -a` exports what the env file defines, so DATABASE_URL reaches the
# script. The env file is the same one deploy/2llazy-ingest.service reads.

# 17 5,13,21 * * *  2llazy  cd /opt/2llazy && set -a && . /etc/2llazy/ingest.env && set +a && flock -n /run/lock/2llazy-ingest.lock sh -c './node_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/ingest.ts --country CZ; ./node_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/ingest.ts --country DE' >> /var/log/2llazy/ingest.log 2>&1

# ── The log file ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create it before the first run, or cron writes nothing and says nothing:
#
#   sudo install -d -o 2llazy -g 2llazy /var/log/2llazy
#
# And rotate it, as /etc/logrotate.d/2llazy:
#
#   /var/log/2llazy/ingest.log {
#       weekly
#       rotate 8
#       compress
#       missingok
#       notifempty
#       copytruncate
#   }
